            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "arrays != lists, and `vim.iter` special-cases (in some cases forcibly) the latter, not the former.\n\nIf an array is coerced to a list, the keys are of course reindexed (precisely to make it a list).\n\n(I know, it's confusing, but it's relatively standard terminology in Lualand that predates Neovim -- coming from other, numeric, languages, I would have called the _latter_ \"arrays\" and the former \"sparse arrays\".)\n",
